WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.189
These giant tech companies have

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.018
so much power,

00:00:04.019 --> 00:00:05.909
Big Tech poses the single

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.859
greatest threat to free speech

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.485
in our country today.

00:00:08.486 --> 00:00:10.409
So much economic power

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.239
and so much political power.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.919
Everywhere you turn these days, big

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.719
tech companies are under fire.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.699
Instagram supposedly addictive

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.259
and negative effects on teenage

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.879
girls have lawmakers comparing its

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.799
parent company, Facebook, to

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.849
Big Tobacco.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.649
Conservatives like Florida Gov.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.779
Ron DeSantis and Texas Gov.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.039
Greg Abbott have signed

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.049
controversial legislation banning

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.609
social media platforms from

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.589
moderating content and kicking off

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.359
users for political reasons.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.219
Supreme Court Associate Justice

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.619
Clarence Thomas has said businesses

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.619
like

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:51.079
Twitter and YouTube should be subject to strict federal regulation. Liberal legislators in Colorado have proposed creating a digital communications commission that would have the power to change how platforms do business in the name of fighting hate speech and misinformation. Lawmakers in at least 38 states have introduced over 100 laws in the past couple of years to regulate online speech and business practices. In his new book, "Tech Panic," Reason's, Robby Soave says such attacks are modern

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.199
day witch hunts that fall apart

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.539
under even mild scrutiny.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.489
They're, the contemporary version of

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.379
past freak outs over video

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.629
games, rock music and comic books.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.219
We shouldn't fear Facebook or the

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.319
future, writes Soave, the actual

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.239
threat, he says, comes not from

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.799
private companies, but from

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.659
politicians, woke mobs,

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.299
social conservatives and activists

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.669
whose real goal is to limit speech

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:36.670
they don't like.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.299
Robby Soave, thanks for talking.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.079
My pleasure.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.029
Give me the elevator pitch

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.169
of "Tech Panic.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.479
Why We Shouldn't Fear Facebook

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.349
and the Future."

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.179
Sure. Panic about social media

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.019
is very popular right now.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.329
