00:53:02.400 --> 00:53:03.719
Facebook and the other social media

00:53:03.720 --> 00:53:05.459
sites are just saying they want to

00:53:05.460 --> 00:53:06.749
go along with regulation.

00:53:06.750 --> 00:53:07.649
But then what does that actually

00:53:07.650 --> 00:53:08.759
look like? You know they want to.

00:53:08.760 --> 00:53:10.079
We're open to it. We're open to it.

00:53:10.080 --> 00:53:12.269
The right regulation when we hadn't

00:53:12.270 --> 00:53:13.889
had input on and made sure was not

00:53:13.890 --> 00:53:15.299
the bad one that we didn't want.

00:53:15.300 --> 00:53:16.589
So there's there's a certain amount

00:53:16.590 --> 00:53:18.089
of cynicism I take with,

00:53:18.090 --> 00:53:20.309
you know, the subtitle of tech panic

00:53:20.310 --> 00:53:22.019
is why we shouldn't fear Facebook,

00:53:22.020 --> 00:53:23.189
which we've talked about and we

00:53:23.190 --> 00:53:24.929
shouldn't fear the future.

00:53:24.930 --> 00:53:27.179
How do we get past the kind of panic

00:53:27.180 --> 00:53:29.219
stage with social media

00:53:29.220 --> 00:53:30.519
or with Big Tech right now?

00:53:30.520 --> 00:53:31.589
What what?

00:53:31.590 --> 00:53:33.059
What are the ways that we can kind

00:53:33.060 --> 00:53:35.099
of moderate, you know, people's

00:53:35.100 --> 00:53:36.839
visceral reactions

00:53:36.840 --> 00:53:39.179
people need to train themselves

00:53:39.180 --> 00:53:40.799
to just like not believe what the

00:53:40.800 --> 00:53:42.719
media is saying about any of these

00:53:42.720 --> 00:53:44.939
things? I really the mainstream

00:53:44.940 --> 00:53:46.469
media is the villain of this book

00:53:46.470 --> 00:53:47.909
and is the villain of so much that's

00:53:47.910 --> 00:53:49.889
going on that the

00:53:49.890 --> 00:53:51.479
narrative that they advance that

00:53:51.480 --> 00:53:52.739
everything new is scary and

00:53:52.740 --> 00:53:53.999
dangerous because it competes with

00:53:54.000 --> 00:53:54.819
them.

00:53:54.820 --> 00:53:56.729
Yeah, they clubhouse the this

00:53:56.730 --> 00:53:59.399
popular audio

00:53:59.400 --> 00:54:01.319
kind of group social

00:54:01.320 --> 00:54:03.299
media app that was really

00:54:03.300 --> 00:54:04.979
briefly popular during the pandemic

00:54:04.980 --> 00:54:05.849
because it was a way to chat with

00:54:05.850 --> 00:54:07.739
people. Know The New York Times

00:54:07.740 --> 00:54:09.959
has this just absurd coverage

00:54:09.960 --> 00:54:11.339
of this thing like, well, what if

00:54:11.340 --> 00:54:12.429
it's not going to recorded?

00:54:12.430 --> 00:54:13.799
So what if people are saying

00:54:13.800 --> 00:54:14.759
they can say whatever they

00:54:14.760 --> 00:54:16.169
want to say, whatever they want is a

00:54:16.170 --> 00:54:17.969
fact check end of the world like

00:54:17.970 --> 00:54:20.399
that kind of that is moral panic.

00:54:20.400 --> 00:54:22.169
And it has been the bread and butter

00:54:22.170 --> 00:54:24.119
of newspapers of local

00:54:24.120 --> 00:54:26.279
television of, you know,

00:54:26.280 --> 00:54:27.389
what are your what are your

00:54:27.390 --> 00:54:29.129
neighbors doing its be afraid for

00:54:29.130 --> 00:54:31.199
your children, that kind of thing.

00:54:31.200 --> 00:54:32.849
That's why I call it a panic.

00:54:32.850 --> 00:54:34.859
And, you know, and all

00:54:34.860 --> 00:54:36.299
of that, so many of those in the

00:54:36.300 --> 00:54:38.279
past have turned out to be

00:54:38.280 --> 00:54:40.319
nothing to them from from

00:54:40.320 --> 00:54:42.599
video games to to the radio

